A release published from `develop` also feeds the S3 Helm repositories and wire-builds, besides Quay and the release managers. A pre-release pushes its charts to `charts-develop` and pins them in the `dev` branch of wire-builds. A GA pushes them to `charts` and pins them in the `main` branch only, `dev` is left alone. A pin never moves backwards: `dev` is not changed when it already pins a newer commit, and `main` refuses a version lower than the one it pins. Every chart of the release is packaged when the candidate is prepared and checked against its checksum before anything is published. If the S3 or wire-builds step fails, the `Publish legacy channels` workflow runs it again for the published release. A release from a `release/X.Y` branch only goes to Quay and the release managers.
